        "quote": "In an action to recover damages for personal injuries, the defendant New York Food & Drink Flushing, Inc., appeals, as limited by its brief, from so much of an order of the Supreme Court, Queens County (McDonald, J.), dated May 1, 2012, as denied its motion pursuant to CPLR 3211 (a) to dismiss the complaint insofar as asserted against it.",
        "statement_status": "procedural_history"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E002",
        "passage_id": "P001",
        "quote": "Ordered that the order is affirmed insofar as appealed from, without costs or disbursements.",
        "statement_status": "current_disposition"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E003",
        "passage_id": "P001",
        "quote": "The plaintiff allegedly slipped and/or tripped and fell at or near certain premises located in Flushing, which were owned by the defendant Diamond Hill Realty, LLC (hereinafter Diamond Hill). As a result, the plaintiff commenced this action against, among others, Diamond Hill and the defendant New York Food & Drink Flushing, Inc. (hereinafter New York Food), the alleged tenant of the premises.",
        "statement_status": "allegation"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E004",
        "passage_id": "P003",
        "quote": "Here, the affidavits submitted by New York Food were not proper documentary evidence, and its submission of the stipulation of settlement between Diamond Hill and the purported holdover tenant failed to conclusively establish that it was not in possession of the premises at the time of the accident.",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E005",
        "passage_id": "P005",
        "quote": "Here, contrary to New York Food’s contention, the affidavits of its vice president and the stipulation of settlement between Diamond Hill and the purported holdover tenant did not demonstrate that no significant dispute exists as to whether it had assumed control over the premises at the time of the accident.",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E006",
        "passage_id": "P001",
        "quote": "Prior to serving an answer, New York Food moved pursuant to CPLR 3211 (a) (1) and (7) to dismiss the complaint insofar as asserted against it, contending that, at the time of the accident, it had not yet taken possession of the premises because the premises were occupied by a holdover tenant.",
        "statement_status": "party_argument"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E007",
        "passage_id": "P003",
        "quote": "Contrary to New York Food’s contention, affidavits do not qualify as “documentary evidence” for purposes of a motion to dismiss pursuant to CPLR 3211 (a) (1)",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E008",
        "passage_id": "P005",
        "quote": "Accordingly, the Supreme Court properly denied New York Food’s motion pursuant to CPLR 3211 (a) (1) and (7) to dismiss the complaint insofar as asserted against it.",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      }
